## Known partial-limitation commands (Era 1 V3, available-but-limited)

- `ai connect`: API-key authentication is not implemented by the local daemon; falls back to subscription sign-in (commands/ai/connect.go:112).

## Commands needing an explicit public-vs-internal classification

(`Hidden: true` in source — Era 10 V34 / Era 11 V39 own the decision)

- `admin`: `admin` (commands/admin/admin.go:11)
- `admin`: `connect-edge-node` (commands/admin/admin.go:17)
- `admin`: `bootstrap` (commands/admin/bootstrap.go:19)
- `mcpcmd`: `mcp-serve` (commands/mcpcmd/mcpcmd.go:48)

## Known extraction gap: `output.RegisterFlags()` shared flags (Era 2 V7)

The flag counts above come from literal `Flags().Kind("name", ...)` call sites
inside `commands/`. They do **not** include `--json`, `--output`, `--quiet`,
`--yes`, `--wait`, `--timeout` on the **196 commands** that attach them via one
indirect call, `output.RegisterFlags(cmd)` (`beaver-cli/output/output.go`,
outside `commands/` — confirmed by a live source scan (direct calls and the
`for _, c := range []*cobra.Command{...}` loop form both counted; re-run by this
script every regeneration, not a hardcoded figure — see `gaps/00-index.docs`
entry 009). Every one of those 196 commands has 6 more flags than this file's
per-group table shows. Documented authoritatively in `cli/shared-flags.mdx`.
Phase 2 family eras should check `grep -rn output.RegisterFlags commands/<group>/`
before assuming a command has no `--wait`/`--json`/etc. just because it's absent
from `commands.csv`.

